==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|bindanan|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|bʰendʰ-||bind|lang=ine-pro}}.  Cognate with Old High German [[bintan]] (German [[binden]]), Old Norse [[binda]] (Swedish [[binda]]), Middle Low German ''binden'' (Dutch [[binden]]).  The Indo-European root was also the source of Avestan ''bendayaiti'' and Greek {{l/grc|πεῖσμα}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbindɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=III}}

# to [[bind]], [[constrain]]
# to [[fasten]] or [[join]]

====Conjugation====
{{ang-conj-strong-IIIa|b|nd}}

====Descendants====
* English: [[bind]]

